### xfactory-dashboard.service — boot-start and restart for the local ideation plane.
###
### INERT ON THIS HOST AS SHIPPED. Measured 2026-08-13: /etc/wsl.conf carries
### `[boot] systemd=false`, PID 1 is `init(Ubuntu-24.04)`, and `systemctl --user`
### answers "System has not been booted with systemd as init system. Can't
### operate." So this unit cannot start until systemd is enabled — it is committed
### ready, not committed working, and that distinction is the point of this
### header. `reserve-dashboard.sh --supervise` is the restart-on-crash path that
### works TODAY; it does not survive a reboot, which is what this unit is for.
###
### TO ENABLE (needs root once, and restarts every WSL session):
###   1. set `systemd=true` under `[boot]` in /etc/wsl.conf
###   2. from Windows: `wsl --shutdown`, then reopen the distro
###   3. mkdir -p ~/.config/systemd/user
###      ln -s <repo>/scripts/systemd/xfactory-dashboard.service \
###            ~/.config/systemd/user/xfactory-dashboard.service
###   4. systemctl --user daemon-reload
###      systemctl --user enable --now xfactory-dashboard
###   5. loginctl enable-linger "$USER"      # start at boot, not at first login
###
### Step 5 is not optional for the stated goal. Without lingering a user unit
### starts when the user first logs in, so a power cut with nobody logged in
### leaves the dashboard down — the exact failure this is meant to end.
###
### WITHOUT SYSTEMD there are two other boot-start routes, both outside this file:
###   * /etc/wsl.conf `[boot] command=` — runs as root at WSL start; would need to
###     drop to the owning user before serving. Root edit, `wsl --shutdown`.
###   * Windows Task Scheduler at logon running `wsl.exe -u <user> -- <script>`.
###     No root, but it is Windows-side configuration and invisible from here.
###
### ExecStart points at the script, never at a remembered argument list: the
### script derives the plane, the register and one --source-root per published
### repository, so this unit cannot drift from what the plane actually contains.

[Unit]
Description=xFactory ideation dashboard (local multi-repository plane)
Documentation=file:%h/projects/xFactory/openxFactory/docs/ideation-dashboard-session-runbook.md
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=exec
# EDIT THIS PATH if the runtime lives in a different checkout. It is deliberately
# not derived: a unit that guesses its own working tree is worse than one that
# states it.
ExecStart=%h/projects/xFactory/openxFactory-worktrees/change-add-wheel-action-verbs/scripts/reserve-dashboard.sh
Restart=always
RestartSec=3
# The serve binds loopback only and writes into the checkout the gate acts on;
# it is not hardened further here because gate verbs legitimately write there.
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
